{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/671583-sorcerers-do-you-use-those-guys-in-your-games-and-if-you-do-how","id":671583,"title":"Sorcerers, do you use those guys in your games and if you do, how?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-09-19T18:36:50-07:00","id":671583,"title":"Sorcerers, do you use those guys in your games and if you do, how?","content":"Aeon Rites, Balamob, Nephite Priesthood, Thal'Hun, Uzoma, Asatru Futhark, Pythian Order, Fenian, Mogen Ha Chav, Seven Thunders, Dreamers of the Silver Portal... does anyone still remember those societies and plays with their mysteries, agendas and intrigues?<br /> <br /> Just because the forums seem awfully silent about them, a little thread to show good, old WoD: Sorcerer &amp; its revised edition some love. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Come and bring your thoughts and stories those who would like to talk about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T19:35:42-07:00","id":671617,"title":"","content":"The forums are a bit quiet after a slew of.... not so happy loudness about them. There are some very strong feelings about Sorcerers, and if integrating them into Mage was a good thing, or a bad thing.<br /> <br /> They do get regular use in my cWOD games that are mortal, hunter (any stripe), or Mage focused.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T19:57:26-07:00","id":671622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/671583-sorcerers-do-you-use-those-guys-in-your-games-and-if-you-do-how?p=671617#post671617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The forums are a bit quiet after a slew of.... not so happy loudness about them. There are some very strong feelings about Sorcerers, and if integrating them into Mage was a good thing, or a bad thing.<br /> <br /> They do get regular use in my cWOD games that are mortal, hunter (any stripe), or Mage focused.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm quite surprised to know there was such level of heated disagreement over them, but then i never read Revised edition and have no idea of how that turned out.<br /> <br /> Though i kind of understand those who might prefer Sorcerer to stand on its own outside Ascension, as i used them far more as &quot;quick-&amp;-dirty alternative&quot; to the<br /> Awakened in some of my VtM or hunter games, among other things because i felt more confortable with fitting them in those. but then it's a matter of taste and sticking<br /> or not to the books in the end.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T01:42:38-07:00","id":671724,"title":"","content":"Since Hedge-Magic is so large, it basically can replicate near to any effect you`d want, they feature quite prominently in most of my games.<br /> Many of my Players have at least dabbled in hedge-magic, I use hedge-magic as inspiration for spirit powers, and whatever bad dude they are fighting could be a big scary evil ancient monster... or a hedge-magican with just the right pathes to replicate their powers.<br /> Of course this goes both ways, and what seems to be &quot;just&quot; an insufferable cult-leader with some minor hedge magic could turn out to be something else entirely.<br /> Personaly I like it, when my players are not too sure about what they are facing on a metagame-level.<br /> <br /> Scotish looking dude transformes into a wolflike creature and talks to evil spirits? Surely it can`t be anything else than a Black Spiral dancer...<br /> Or maybe its an awakend mage with a dark nature paradigem, a possessed mortal (Fomori), a Thrall to a demon if not one himself, an old fae from a bygone age, an upstart infernalist<br /> or: a Sorcerer with either Shapechanging and Spirit-Talk or Illusion Magic.<br /> <br /> This keeps them on their toes and makes sure, that the players don`t know all the answers from the beginning, just because they read the apropiate rule-book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6112-seki","name":"Seki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T04:40:07-07:00","id":671815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/671583-sorcerers-do-you-use-those-guys-in-your-games-and-if-you-do-how?p=671724#post671724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since Hedge-Magic is so large, it basically can replicate near to any effect you`d want, they feature quite prominently in most of my games.<br /> Many of my Players have at least dabbled in hedge-magic, I use hedge-magic as inspiration for spirit powers, and whatever bad dude they are fighting could be a big scary evil ancient monster... or a hedge-magican with just the right pathes to replicate their powers.<br /> Of course this goes both ways, and what seems to be &quot;just&quot; an insufferable cult-leader with some minor hedge magic could turn out to be something else entirely.<br /> Personaly I like it, when my players are not too sure about what they are facing on a metagame-level.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah, their magic system is plenty flexible and it can be quite pratical for those times when you don't care to bring up a big book with you just for spirit or some other supernatural's tricks. In fact the WoD: Sorcerer had a vagrant girl who would occasionally turn into an occasionally man-eating feline among its sample characters, for example.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/671583-sorcerers-do-you-use-those-guys-in-your-games-and-if-you-do-how?p=671724#post671724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Scotish looking dude transformes into a wolflike creature and talks to evil spirits? Surely it can`t be anything else than a Black Spiral dancer...</div> </div> </div> </div>Jason Statham? No, wait, he's british, forget it... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/671583-sorcerers-do-you-use-those-guys-in-your-games-and-if-you-do-how?p=671724#post671724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or maybe its an awakend mage with a dark nature paradigem, a possessed mortal (Fomori), a Thrall to a demon if not one himself, an old fae from a bygone age, an upstart infernalist<br /> or: a Sorcerer with either Shapechanging and Spirit-Talk or Illusion Magic.<br /> <br /> This keeps them on their toes and makes sure, that the players don`t know all the answers from the beginning, just because they read the aproppiate rule-book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hehehehehe - i have done some fudging of my own too, like alchemists coming up with potions from Mummy's alchemy or the occasional society of sorcerers with one or two rites taken from stuff in Dead Magic or the Book of Madness, just for fun.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 12-05-2015, 09:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T10:42:21-07:00","id":672206,"title":"","content":"As a player: I especially used them when I was unable to make regular gaming sessions. It allowed me to play a character that could drop in and out of the regular story, and add to it without eclipsing the regular players. Bastet Kin that was a Shaman and could facilitate spirit dealings for younger trueborns, creating magical artifacts for Vampires, etc.<br /> <br /> As an ST, a way to change\u200b things up and make things up that players don't expect. People with fangs and snake powers... that are immune to sunlight! (That got a Corax Player.)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","name":"EvilTyger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T11:34:53-07:00","id":672252,"title":"","content":"As antagonists and neutral characters. Mages are to complicated to give most werewolf players NPC instructions for, since they are too damn flexible and one has to understand the whole paradigm thing and all that, so no mages. But sorcerers are easy usable and easy to write instructions for and define their powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T14:03:08-07:00","id":672357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/671583-sorcerers-do-you-use-those-guys-in-your-games-and-if-you-do-how?p=672252#post672252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As antagonists and neutral characters. Mages are to complicated to give most werewolf players NPC instructions for, since they are too damn flexible and one has to understand the whole paradigm thing and all that, so no mages. But sorcerers are easy usable and easy to write instructions for and define their powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, quickness to use is a must with them.<br /> <br /> As a player i have used a young Thal'hun who struck as a reasonably sucessful musician and used his work and shows as part propaganda, part experiments in perfecting his knowledge and skills with <i>thal</i> (magic), what has made him one of their most visible members and effective recruiter, with even a few contacts among other occult societies and a few supernatural encounters. These in particular shocked him considerably and he has taken it upon himself to collect data on this subject, that he has discovered to be apparently quite a considerable blindspot of his brethen in relation to other groups.<br /> <br /> This would be both the hook that lead him to the group - a investigators-hunters sort of mixed crew - but also to some interesting subplot in the form of a Void Engineer who saw one of his shows while in a sci-fi convention and developed a personal interest in the character and the Thal'hun.<br /> <br /> The positive side of it was that, as the PC struck a sort of friendship with her and she learned more of the society, she slowly convinced other figures in the Technocracy that they weren't an etherite branch and that hunting them down wouldn't serve their cause.<br /> <br /> The negative was that she actually believed Khuvon and the Jeva to be signs of Umbrood infiltration and that by giving them - and specially the PC - some breathing room they might better detect and nip the invasion at the bud, possibly using his own discoveries about the supernatural to subtle convince him and other brethen of the dangers of Jeva corruption and eventual turnaround of the Thal'hun into a Technocracy tool. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> There was also some crazy parallel stuff like a daughter of cacophony stalker that was divided about embracing him or not and, much more scaringly, the agents of a eastern True Hand elder that learned of the society during the &quot;Middle East incident&quot; where a ambassador mission of theirs in the region ended up dead. He suspected the sorcerers might be agents of Underworld forces trying to oppose Enoch or some form of indirect tool of the Aralu or even the Antediluvians and intended to locate a number of Thal'hun through the PC's movements to then be ghouled into informants and agents of his own in the society (the PC in particular was seen as too public a person to make the kind of discrete tool the elder required).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 12-05-2015, 09:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T16:42:57-07:00","id":672480,"title":"","content":"I can see Sorcerer being a good way to get someone completely new to WoD and Mage in particular used to the game. Their Paths are linear, so anyone coming off a game like DnD, or even someone who has never played a tabletop RPG, won't be overwhelmed like they would with Mage's Sphere system. But the Paths can be open-ended enough in some cases (I'm looking at you, Alchemy and Enchantment) that it can ease them into the ideas that Spheres are based on.<br /> <br /> Moreover, playing an unAwakened Sorcerer is just simpler than other character types. One of the things nWoD did right was starting with a book for completely vanilla play, that then formed the basis for all other gamelines. So you could play regular humans, without the ancillary details about playing the various splats that complicate things. So with Sorcerer, players don't need to worry about things like Blood Pool/Humanity/Frenzy, Rage/Gnosis/different forms, Arete/Focus/Quintessence/Paradox, etc. Those sorts of things can be overwhelming, especially for new players.<br /> <br /> If nothing else, it'd be nice to run a game of Mage, but without Paradox hanging like the sword of Damacles over the players' heads. Path magic doesn't excite the wrath of the Consensus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T17:14:07-07:00","id":672547,"title":"","content":"In my chronicles, I typically have various people out there who know some kind of magic that may come into contact with the PCs. If the players focus on the occult, they may end up encountering people who know magic I make up on the fly. Mechanically, all these people are Sorcerers - and I typically limit them to the Paths in the original Sorcerer books, or the various Infernalist Paths in the Vampire game.<br /> <br /> I don't use the actual organizations found in the WoD: Sorcerer Book and find a way to tell a story with them. However, I will use the name and concept of the organization for these NPCs if they &quot;fit&quot; what I want to do anyway. If an organization, name, and backstory already exists, it saves me time and gives it a more &quot;World of Darkness&quot; feel than if I created my own.<ul><li>The Ancient Order of the Aeon Rites - whenever I need an organization that is essentially the Golden Dawn and Aleister Crowley, I use these guys.</li> <li>Uzoma - If I ever need an indigenous African sorcerer, I use them.</li> <li>Mogen Ha Chav - if I need Kabbalists with real magical power, I use them.</li> <li>Seven Thunders - I have only ever used them as part of historical backstory or lore if the PCs are investigating something's history.</li> <li>Dreamers of the Silver Portal - I use them for any plot I run that is inspired by Lovecraft's Dream Cycle.</li> </ul><br /> I have used the Aeon Rites and Silver Portal the most. I have inserted the Uzoma and Mogen in a chronicle sandbox, but they never came up. The Thunders have only been mentioned when the old professor, antiquarian, occultist, or Mentor was giving the PCs an info dump.<br /> <br /> I haven't used any of the others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T18:34:41-07:00","id":672666,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/671583-sorcerers-do-you-use-those-guys-in-your-games-and-if-you-do-how?p=672547#post672547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my chronicles, I typically have various people out there who know some kind of magic that may come into contact with the PCs. If the players focus on the occult, they may end up encountering people who know magic I make up on the fly. Mechanically, all these people are Sorcerers - and I typically limit them to the Paths in the original Sorcerer books, or the various Infernalist Paths in the Vampire game.<br /> <br /> I don't use the actual organizations found in the WoD: Sorcerer Book and find a way to tell a story with them. However, I will use the name and concept of the organization for these NPCs if they &quot;fit&quot; what I want to do anyway. If an organization, name, and backstory already exists, it saves me time and gives it a more &quot;World of Darkness&quot; feel than if I created my own.<ul><li>The Ancient Order of the Aeon Rites - whenever I need an organization that is essentially the Golden Dawn and Aleister Crowley, I use these guys.</li> <li>Uzoma - If I ever need an indigenous African sorcerer, I use them.</li> <li>Mogen Ha Chav - if I need Kabbalists with real magical power, I use them.</li> <li>Seven Thunders - I have only ever used them as part of historical backstory or lore if the PCs are investigating something's history.</li> <li>Dreamers of the Silver Portal - I use them for any plot I run that is inspired by Lovecraft's Dream Cycle.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> I have used the Aeon Rites and Silver Portal the most. I have inserted the Uzoma and Mogen in a chronicle sandbox, but they never came up. The Thunders have only been mentioned when the old professor, antiquarian, occultist, or Mentor was giving the PCs an info dump.<br /> <br /> I haven't used any of the others.</div> </div> </div> </div>Truth be told, using just the concept is the pratical thing for any game where you don't have some hooks in mind for one piece or another of an organization's background. They are all samples anyway, as big or small as one cares to make them. Beside them i have adapted some real groups, made up my own and stolen from other books (like some cults in the Book of Madness and two Golden Dawn style covens in Dark Colony).<br /> <br /> In the &quot;occult trobuleshooters&quot; game i mentioned above we had interactions with Aeon Rites, Arcanum (that half the group saw as a stodgier version of the Aeons), Uzoma in the two sides of the Atlantic (beside some societies that bartardized uzoma rites with golden dawn style magic, mediunism and other weirdness), the Fenian, the Pythian Order, Silver Portal and the Asatru Futhark.<br /> <br /> Of these we got the most milleage out of Uzoma (there's a reason i mention the two sides of the Atlantic and weird derivatives in Brasil), Pythian Order &amp; Silver Portal (whom my character developed a little obsession with due to similarities of some interest &amp; myths respectively) and the Asatru - that the ST intended as a one-shot with a disciple and his skinhead friends messing a show in Amsterdam, but somehow scalated in crazy ways into a insane bloodbath of a story arc and a semi-regular nemesis of the group after that. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-27T00:17:11-07:00","id":679725,"title":"","content":"I have used the Seven Thunders in a few chronicles. I find having someone as flexible as Soccers as an antagonist keeps both the players and myself on my toes. My favorite example is the Socceress that I used in my last chronicle. She was sly and malevolent her actions included: convincing a vampire she was harmless, binding her slain lovers to her house to serve as guardians, accusing a werewolf's kin of rape, and escaping twice from the very angry pack of my Werewolf players.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-27T06:46:52-07:00","id":679937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lncbill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/671583-sorcerers-do-you-use-those-guys-in-your-games-and-if-you-do-how?p=679725#post679725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have used the Seven Thunders in a few chronicles. I find having someone as flexible as <b>Soccers</b> as an antagonist keeps both the players and myself on my toes.</div> </div> </div> </div>They can be surprisingly quick on their feet, no? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lncbill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/671583-sorcerers-do-you-use-those-guys-in-your-games-and-if-you-do-how?p=679725#post679725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My favorite example is the Socceress that I used in my last chronicle. She was sly and malevolent her actions included: <b>convincing a vampire she was harmless</b>, binding her slain lovers to her house to serve as guardians, accusing a werewolf's kin of rape, and escaping twice from the very angry pack of my Werewolf players.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, while certainly sly and dishonest that isn't quite malevolent on itself - depends on what she does with this lie after convincing the vamp.... and anyone with sense would try to escape from an angry pack of garou. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> As an aside, the rape false accusation makes me think of the crazy stalker arsonist crush from the 2nd season of Dexter. Fun times.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-29T07:20:59-07:00","id":682019,"title":"","content":"Malevolent-she murdered the bound dead lovers to the house that she stole from one. The Vampire was her lover, as well as a meal ticket. Unfortunately for both the Werewolf pack, i.e. my players were fond of the kinfolk accused of rape and were determined to prove his innocence. Even a Socceress and Vampire should be afraid of a pack of 5 Garou they also should've invested in silver bullets","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-29T07:29:30-07:00","id":682024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lncbill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/671583-sorcerers-do-you-use-those-guys-in-your-games-and-if-you-do-how?p=682019#post682019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Malevolent-she murdered the bound dead lovers to the house that she stole from one. The Vampire was her lover, as well as a meal ticket. Unfortunately for both the Werewolf pack, i.e. my players were fond of the kinfolk accused of rape and were determined to prove his innocence. Even a Socceress and Vampire should be afraid of a pack of 5 Garou they also should've invested in silver bullets</div> </div> </div> </div>A vampire would have to be pretty suicidal or ridiculously powerful <b>not</b> to be affraid of a pack of 5 Garou. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-29T09:29:13-07:00","id":682158,"title":"","content":"I prefer using hedge magic for cross-over purposes when I need to represent willworkers. I don't really use them as parts of organizations unless it is vaguely related to the Order of Reason/Technocracy (generally to impress on my pack the growing power of the Weaver). The Mage paradigm is interesting but their powers are overbearing and I have little interest in my magically-inclined NPCs running rough-shod over my player characters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3695,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","user":"The Laughing Stranger","date":". 10-05-2015, 01:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T05:02:52-07:00","id":682998,"title":"","content":"I prefer not to use actual rules for NPC sorcerors/mages. I don't differentiate them in character, and I give them whatever I need for their narrative purposes. I tend to define them as a paradigm, and then just wing their effects with similar guidelines as M:tA characters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-01T06:00:31-07:00","id":684342,"title":"","content":"I don't particularly care for the way Rites work so i use a lot of the rules from Sorcerer Revised linear magic into Rites. So Summoning/Binding/Warding Rituals are used in place of Rite of Summoning Spirit and Rites for making Talons, Fetishes, and even the occasional Possessed. Its uncommon but I also normally have a few kinfolk shamans that have some knowledge things like Alchemy and/or Enchantment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-01T06:09:29-07:00","id":684347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Derzhuzad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/671583-sorcerers-do-you-use-those-guys-in-your-games-and-if-you-do-how?p=684342#post684342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't particularly care for the way Rites work so i use a lot of the rules from Sorcerer Revised linear magic into Rites. So Summoning/Binding/Warding Rituals are used in place of Rite of Summoning Spirit and Rites for making Talons, Fetishes, and even the occasional Possessed. Its uncommon but I also normally have a few kinfolk shamans that have some knowledge things like Alchemy and/or Enchantment.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not familiar with them at the moment, what are the main differences?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-01T06:16:26-07:00","id":684355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/671583-sorcerers-do-you-use-those-guys-in-your-games-and-if-you-do-how?p=684347#post684347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not familiar with them at the moment, what are the main differences?</div> </div> </div> </div>More crunch, less fluff. Rites are mostly loosley defined and governed by a single roll. Sorcerous spells have specific effects charts, guidelines and difficulties. I honestly prefer the Rites.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-01T07:36:46-07:00","id":684425,"title":"","content":"Basically what Asmodai said. Rites have a single all encompassing system confined in each of their effect. With the single Rite of Summoning a Garou can summon any spirit they want theoretically. The difficulty changes based on the strength of the spirit you wish to summon, your adherence to their taboo's, and amount of time spent preparing while the time it takes for the spirit to respond and its general mood that you summoned it is decided by the number of the success you get. Sorcery version pretty much works the same way but its broken down into multiple levels that requires more investment on the players part to achieve the same results.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-01T08:52:59-07:00","id":684502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Derzhuzad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/671583-sorcerers-do-you-use-those-guys-in-your-games-and-if-you-do-how?p=684425#post684425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Basically what Asmodai said. Rites have a single all encompassing system confined in each of their effect. With the single Rite of Summoning a Garou can summon any spirit they want theoretically. The difficulty changes based on the strength of the spirit you wish to summon, your adherence to their taboo's, and amount of time spent preparing while the time it takes for the spirit to respond and its general mood that you summoned it is decided by the number of the success you get. Sorcery version pretty much works the same way but its broken down into multiple levels that requires more investment on the players part to achieve the same results.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmm, might be interesting to get a PDF copy at drivethru for future reference and curiosity's sake...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-01T09:06:28-07:00","id":684515,"title":"","content":"I prefer the segmented approach, as handing players something they can use to summon a <i>god</i> at Rank 2 with player-adjustable difficulty numbers does not sit well with me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-01T10:10:09-07:00","id":684591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/671583-sorcerers-do-you-use-those-guys-in-your-games-and-if-you-do-how?p=684515#post684515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I prefer the segmented approach, as handing players something they can use to summon a <i>god</i> at Rank 2 with player-adjustable difficulty numbers does not sit well with me.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can see your point, even considered it in fact - that said Werewolf already does that sort of thing with its own rite system, the mystic initiate that out of ego and ambition ends up biting far more than it could ever chew is something of a classic (young John Constantine with Nergal for just one example) <b>and</b> comparing both takes does open room for a ST to tinker with both models and consider details and takes one might not otherwise...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-01T14:28:33-07:00","id":684886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/671583-sorcerers-do-you-use-those-guys-in-your-games-and-if-you-do-how?p=684515#post684515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I prefer the segmented approach, as handing players something they can use to summon a <i>god</i> at Rank 2 with player-adjustable difficulty numbers does not sit well with me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Being able to cast something doesn't mean you have the hubris to do so. Even if the Great Things respond you sure as hell should be ready to justify why you are wasting their time and what they will get out of it. That pretty much means that every idiot who decided to randomly summon Incarna and totems for crap learns pretty fast why you should not fuck with things you are not ready for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-01T15:38:32-07:00","id":684964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/671583-sorcerers-do-you-use-those-guys-in-your-games-and-if-you-do-how?p=684886#post684886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Being able to cast something doesn't mean you have the hubris to do so. Even if the Great Things respond you sure as hell should be ready to justify why you are wasting their time and what they will get out of it. That pretty much means that every idiot who decided to randomly summon Incarna and totems for crap learns pretty fast why you should not fuck with things you are not ready for.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see your point - being hypothetically possible doesn't mean an individual magician actually knows how or that it is (over)confident enough to seriously try.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-04T06:03:57-07:00","id":688172,"title":"","content":"Exactly. In addition to that, I personally rule this Werewolf-Rite as something, that is enabled by the pacts between shifters and spirits.<br /> This means, that its power is actualy based more on social grounds, instead of raw magical power.<br /> The spirits <b>promissed</b> they would come, if summoned in this fashion, they are not <b>forced</b> to do so.<br /> This usually doesn`t make any difference mechanically, since spirits imensely loathe to break a promisse, so they come either way.<br /> <br /> It can however mean, that they can bend themselves within the bounds of their promisse. Especially the effects of the sucesses, the player shaman accomplishes can be wildly interpreted by the storyteller this way. I personally see them as the default for a previosly unaware spirit, that bases his attitude mainly on how convincing and precise the shaman offers his ritual incantations and how flattering for the spirit it comes across (meaning the number of sucesses of the ritual-roll).<br /> A specivic spirit, who knowes the players and or the circumstances of their situation at the time of the call is more or less free to arrive whenever, and in whatever mood he himself seems fit.<br /> Thats not to say, that a lack of sucesses would not anger him, or a lot of sucesses would not flatter him enough, to maybe go a little easier on them than he originally intended (spirits are easily flattered and place high value on getting a tradition like this rite just <i>right</i> after all).<br /> However this would in my book be more akin to a flattering (or rude) greeting, than an automatic &quot;you have to be frindly to me, `cause I performed the rite nicely&quot;. The spirit is still its own entety after all.<br /> <br /> A sorcerers rite however, I imagine more grounded in actual &quot;power&quot; over the spirit.<br /> It <b>forces</b> them to appear, with all the implications, that come from it.<br /> A sufficiently powerfull sorcerer can continue to bind the spirit to his will, overpowering it and force him to do his bidding.<br /> A nicer, more persuasive sorcerer might bargain with the spirit, to help him out of its own free will, making enough sacrifices on his side of the deal, that the spirit overlooks the fact, that it didn`t have much choice in coming.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6112,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6112-seki","user":"Seki","date":". 10-04-2015, 09:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6112-seki","name":"Seki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-05T02:56:57-07:00","id":689521,"title":"","content":"I tend to use them as fringe npcs who can set up contacts with other supernatural groups.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-06T12:33:43-07:00","id":691588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/671583-sorcerers-do-you-use-those-guys-in-your-games-and-if-you-do-how?p=689521#post689521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I tend to use them as fringe npcs who can set up contacts with other supernatural groups.</div> </div> </div> </div>The weird people who know weirder people so to speak, then. Sort of &quot;tip-of-the-iceberg/bridge&quot; between the mundane and supernatural worlds, perharps?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-06T14:45:12-07:00","id":691727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/671583-sorcerers-do-you-use-those-guys-in-your-games-and-if-you-do-how?p=691588#post691588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The weird people who know weirder people so to speak, then. Sort of &amp;quot;tip-of-the-iceberg/bridge&amp;quot; between the mundane and supernatural worlds, perharps?</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, I'm also loathe to run cross over games (don't mix peanut better with my chocolate) so if super natural group A needs to talk to group B I tend to have a weird guy who runs a used book store be the go between unless a pc took an ally or contact in group B.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-06T15:07:37-07:00","id":691748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/671583-sorcerers-do-you-use-those-guys-in-your-games-and-if-you-do-how?p=691727#post691727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Indeed, I'm also loathe to run cross over games (don't mix peanut better with my chocolate) so if super natural group A needs to talk to group B I tend to have a weird guy who runs a used book store be the go between unless a pc took an ally or contact in group B.</div> </div> </div> </div>I get what you mean, sometimes a game simply is not about cross-setting shenanigans or mythology &amp; themes mix up. Have done games with varying degrees of crossing over, sometimes replacing awakened with sorcerers, using Mummy stuff as ancient egyptian magic and the shapeshifters with homebrewed lupines or theriantropes of my own (basically tweaked revenants with Protean and other stuff).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-22T20:19:25-07:00","id":717055,"title":"","content":"When its a game of mostly non-Mages, for that one player who wants to run a mortal spellcaster I prefer using Sorcerer rules. This avoids <i>most </i>of the many crossover rules that have to be dealt with. None of the characters would know the difference between Hedge Magic and True Magick, so using the Traditions with Sorcerer's as Mages works just fine.<br /> <br /> In my home Changeling campaign there are Sorcerers of the Order of Hermes (<a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/House_Merinita\" target=\"_blank\">House Merinita</a>) who are closely allied with the local Changelings. These Sorcerers must be enchanted, have Faerie Blood (4pt Merit) <i>or </i>have skill in Oneiromancy to directly interact with the Dreaming. In such stories, I treat all such Sorcerers have a starting Banality of 3. Most would be considered madmen by today's reckoning. Also, I treat Awareness as Kenning in terms of detecting Chimerical reality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":1756,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","user":"MythAdvocate","date":". 10-23-2015, 09:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T08:04:52-07:00","id":719217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MythAdvocate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/671583-sorcerers-do-you-use-those-guys-in-your-games-and-if-you-do-how?p=717055#post717055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When its a game of mostly non-Mages, for that one player who wants to run a mortal spellcaster I prefer using Sorcerer rules. This avoids <i>most </i>of the many crossover rules that have to be dealt with. None of the characters would know the difference between Hedge Magic and True Magick, so using the Traditions with Sorcerer's as Mages works just fine.<br /> <br /> In my home Changeling campaign there are Sorcerers of the Order of Hermes (<a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/House_Merinita\" target=\"_blank\">House Merinita</a>) who are closely allied with the local Changelings. These Sorcerers must be enchanted, have Faerie Blood (4pt Merit) <i>or </i>have skill in Oneiromancy to directly interact with the Dreaming. In such stories, I treat all such Sorcerers have a starting Banality of 3. Most would be considered madmen by today's reckoning. Also, I treat Awareness as Kenning in terms of detecting Chimerical reality.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, Merinita - so long since i last heard of them. Were they referenced in Mage books or have you played Ars Magica games?<br /> <br /> Your choices are sensible and fit well with the house's tone, as things might have decayed somewhat with the passage of time, but back in the middle ages Faerie Blood was a given within the house, a trait shared by their absolute majority though specific fae type could vary considerably, some might even have a stronger fae nature, as either straight merit or by indirect manifestations like a weakness to iron, having a personal <i>vis</i> source in one's body and a number of other supernatural peculiarities. Oneiromancy makes me think a little more of House Criamon and its oracular/platonic idealist explorations but the skill could certainly fit the Merinitae too and one house being subsumed into the other wouldn't be something out of consideration anyway.<br /> <br /> Damn, and now i'm thinking that House Criamon is an hermetic house that might actually fit amazingly amidst the modern world with its philosophical and physical experimentation tendencies, though keeping them bottled into the Order of Hermes through the centuries might become a veritable uphill battle. I could see them becoming a factor in the spread of Dreamspeakers and the Cult of Ecstasy in western culture. hmmm, ideas, ideas....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 10-23-2015, 11:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T11:16:18-07:00","id":719934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/671583-sorcerers-do-you-use-those-guys-in-your-games-and-if-you-do-how?p=719217#post719217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, Merinita - so long since i last heard of them. Were they referenced in Mage books or have you played Ars Magica games?</div> </div> </div> </div>They are mentioned in the Order of Hermes book, but I originally encountered them in Ars Majica. I take a few liberties in my home campaign, having them <i>mostly </i>have Faerie Blood (the head of the local chapter being a descendant of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Henry_Fuseli\" target=\"_blank\">Henry Fuseli</a>), but the only requirement is for the Sorcerer to be skilled in Oneiromancy (at least one dot). Other favored Paths are Alchemy, Illusion and Mana Manipulation. In the setting (New Sophia, Kingdom of Grass) this society of mages have a friendly history with several groups of local fae. This forged some strong connections during the interregnum.<br /> <br /> House Criamon would also make for an excellent Changeling friendly Craft. I could see them being into Chronomancy, Divination, Fortune and Oneiromancy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T12:35:34-07:00","id":720193,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MythAdvocate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/671583-sorcerers-do-you-use-those-guys-in-your-games-and-if-you-do-how?p=719934#post719934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They are mentioned in the Order of Hermes book, but I originally encountered them in Ars Majica. I take a few liberties in my home campaign, having them <i>mostly </i>have Faerie Blood (the head of the local chapter being a descendant of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Henry_Fuseli\" target=\"_blank\">Henry Fuseli</a>), but the only requirement is for the Sorcerer to be skilled in Oneiromancy (at least one dot). Other favored Paths are Alchemy, Illusion and Mana Manipulation. In the setting (New Sophia, Kingdom of Grass) this society of mages have a friendly history with several groups of local fae. This forged some strong connections during the interregnum.</div> </div> </div> </div>Makes sense the dominance of Fae Blood diminishing somewhat due to increasing difficulty to interact with them directly, so it's pretty fair change.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MythAdvocate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/671583-sorcerers-do-you-use-those-guys-in-your-games-and-if-you-do-how?p=719934#post719934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">House Criamon would also make for an excellent Changeling friendly Craft. I could see them being into Chronomancy, Divination, Fortune and Oneiromancy.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's something to look into, might try to tinker a bit with versions of the Ars Magica-era Houses in contemporary times. Except the Tremere, for obvious setting reasons - and the fact the Order of Hermes' Janissaries are pretty much neo-Tremere with a middle eastern veneer. <img src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T12:25:10-07:00","id":735473,"title":"","content":"(Just jumping in -- glanced over some responses, but didn't read previous pages in any detail...)<br /> <br /> I like Sorcerers, especially as a variant counter-point to what Mages are presented as. In the DA/Ravenloft-hybrid game that I've run on-and-off for some years, I have a fae-blooded (S)orceress PC (the player was/still is new to the WoD, and the Mage game mechanics can get heady; Sorcerer is easy for someone coming from DnD -- as with the player in question -- to adapt to conceptually with little muss/fuss). In-game, there often isn't an immediate differentiation between Awakened Mages and Sorcerers; meta-narratively, the difference in applied metaphysics adds both a different slant on how to approach a character/situation as well as conceptualize how a given character's magic works... or doesn't....<br /> <br /> As far as the game mechanic/thematic differences, I don't have a problem with Sorcerers and Mages running around in a story: some people may have issues with them, but I've never had one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T15:43:09-07:00","id":736034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Just John, Forever...</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/671583-sorcerers-do-you-use-those-guys-in-your-games-and-if-you-do-how?p=735473#post735473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Just jumping in -- glanced over some responses, but didn't read previous pages in any detail...)</div> </div> </div> </div>No prob, discussion and commentary overall has been kind of scattershot anyway. Everybody is kind of a jumper here. <img src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Just John, Forever...</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/671583-sorcerers-do-you-use-those-guys-in-your-games-and-if-you-do-how?p=735473#post735473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like Sorcerers, especially as a variant counter-point to what Mages are presented as. In the DA/Ravenloft-hybrid game that I've run on-and-off for some years, I have a fae-blooded (S)orceress PC (the player was/still is new to the WoD, and the Mage game mechanics can get heady; Sorcerer is easy for someone coming from DnD -- as with the player in question -- to adapt to conceptually with little muss/fuss). In-game, there often isn't an immediate differentiation between Awakened Mages and Sorcerers; meta-narratively, the difference in applied metaphysics adds both a different slant on how to approach a character/situation as well as conceptualize how a given character's magic works... or doesn't....<br /> <br /> As far as the game mechanic/thematic differences, I don't have a problem with Sorcerers and Mages running around in a story: some people may have issues with them, but I've never had one.</div> </div> </div> </div>The homebrew setting makes me remember a discussion in the old forums about doing a fantasy game with Mage the Awakenning and some Second Sight stuff for rules but a mostly made-up setting - there were some entertaining stuff like the idea of awakened magic as supernal spark taken from the gods, spheres as the colors of the spark/flame and Paradox as the pure &amp; simple spiteful wrath of the heavens towards mortals daring to flaunt the stolen legacy. There was also a sword &amp; sorcery one using Requiem's disciplines for magic system, with some gory rituals to convert blood into vitae. Fun stuff.<br /> <br /> Mixing, matching or substituting Mages or Sorcerers is all up to how a ST feels like rolling with the systems. Used spell casters with bastardized thaumaturgy, garou rituals and mummy powers in a bunch of games before Ascension came up - sometimes i will bring them back to the table out of laziness, nostalgia or a bit of both depending on occasion. Brewing can always be fun to bring some ace in the hole or to mess with the occasional fluff-abusing player. <img src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T11:06:44-07:00","id":738990,"title":"","content":"Amongst the groups I've played in, they're quite common. Most GM's I've played Mage allows a Mage to take a merit to give a few dots in Sorcery. I've seen one Order of Hermes Mage who had like 12 dots in Sorcery, most in Hellfire and Weather Control, mix it with his True Magick and wreck a Technocrat base. He just walked in and started tossing Hellfire and supercharging them with Forces 4. He ripped through Hitmarks and Enlightened Agents. The Sorcery made the True Magick not vulgar because he was disguising it as Paradox free magic. Which no one thought of doing before in the Order since Sorcerers are looked down upon with disgust. Don't mess with House Flambeau...<br /> <br /> We customized the Sorcery rules too. Basically you could power spells with Mana (which was just another name for Quintessence) or Willpower. Also made it so Rituals were just basically Rotes that were better in power than the normal spell level. Also made all Paths have Rituals. So really limited free form magic like Mage, but with a few written spells to keep that Spellbook vibe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1VN49Y7tH2ZV0l7Hx65RWX1ez-Q9Lst-8ZTyTJeCTpxM/\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerer 20th</a> homebrew and my update to <a href=\"http://immortalthegathering.blogspot.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Highlander: the Gathering</a> for 20th Anniversary edition.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2414-theoutlander523","name":"theoutlander523","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T11:25:38-07:00","id":739031,"title":"","content":"For my next campain, I`m thinking of letting my Mage-Players have the option of investing in Sorcerer-Paths if they like.<br /> They are quite expensive for the effect they get you, and are extremly riged compared to true magic, but they are Paradox-Free.<br /> So they can have a mixture of paradox-inducing free-form sphere magic and rigid paradox-free path-magic.<br /> Since raising both would require an enormous amount of EXP I don`t think I will see too much abuse happening.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6112-seki","name":"Seki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T22:55:39-07:00","id":740961,"title":"","content":"Honestly I feel sorcerers are fun and worthwhile to integrate into most of the Gamelines. Everything from Giovanni keeping the tradition of Mortal Necromancers, and Setites cultivating Lector Priests to Werewolves girding their kin with Arcane secrets, and of course Mages... Pentex and Technocracy would be very worthwhile to have Enhanced Science style sorcerers, and I even go off the reservation and consider allowing Sorcery as a component of wraiths in the Underworld to put those ruins of the Alexandrian Library to use and the like...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T22:57:07-07:00","id":740965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/671583-sorcerers-do-you-use-those-guys-in-your-games-and-if-you-do-how?p=682024#post682024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A vampire would have to be pretty suicidal or ridiculously powerful <b>not</b> to be affraid of a pack of 5 Garou. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Even a Pack of 6 Garou should be afraid of a Pack of 5 Garou!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T06:08:37-07:00","id":741507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/671583-sorcerers-do-you-use-those-guys-in-your-games-and-if-you-do-how?p=740965#post740965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even a Pack of 6 Garou should be afraid of a Pack of 5 Garou!</div> </div> </div> </div>All too true.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T08:40:21-07:00","id":741937,"title":"","content":"In my gonzo crosssover CWoD i use Sorcerors as the rank and file of the Traditions, Technocracy and other Mage Organizations. True Magi are one in a million and are mysterious Ubermensch to the settings denizens. Sorcerors are the guys who make up the majority of the factions and each of them is seeking Ascension, where they corssover from Sorceror to Magus. It seems to work so far.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1919-muadib","name":"muadib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1919_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T08:52:45-07:00","id":741960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>muadib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/671583-sorcerers-do-you-use-those-guys-in-your-games-and-if-you-do-how?p=741937#post741937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my gonzo crosssover CWoD i use Sorcerors as the rank and file of the Traditions, Technocracy and other Mage Organizations. True Magi are one in a million and are mysterious Ubermensch to the settings denizens. Sorcerors are the guys who make up the majority of the factions and each of them is seeking Ascension, where they corssover from Sorceror to Magus. It seems to work so far.</div> </div> </div> </div>Curiously, nWoD does give a pretty similar set-up in the Second Sight book and some of the stuff that comes after it, mixing up individual and groups dealing with &quot;supernal&quot; and &quot;fallen world&quot; magic, among other stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T10:36:18-07:00","id":742195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/671583-sorcerers-do-you-use-those-guys-in-your-games-and-if-you-do-how?p=741960#post741960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Curiously, nWoD does give a pretty similar set-up in the Second Sight book and some of the stuff that comes after it, mixing up individual and groups dealing with &quot;supernal&quot; and &quot;fallen world&quot; magic, among other stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>I confess i did steal a number of NWoD ideas to incorporate my Gonzo setting. That may have been one of them, but i cant quite recall. There's a lot of great material in the NWoD, especially in light of 2nd ed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1919-muadib","name":"muadib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1919_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T11:50:52-07:00","id":742412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>muadib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/671583-sorcerers-do-you-use-those-guys-in-your-games-and-if-you-do-how?p=742195#post742195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I confess i did steal a number of NWoD ideas to incorporate my Gonzo setting. That may have been one of them, but i cant quite recall. There's a lot of great material in the NWoD, especially in light of 2nd ed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could be so, but could be coincidence too, it's the kind of thing that can happen on its own when working with closely-related ideas and themes - i still remember a little freak-out in an old Aberrant game when we got the Teragen book and their &quot;Chrysalis&quot; concept (a form of transhuman evolution by directed accruing of Taint), that pretty much replicated the background and dark secret of my chraracter, making him the only self-taught 2nd stage Nova and wholy outside Teragen to boot. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-08T19:11:16-08:00","id":761127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/671583-sorcerers-do-you-use-those-guys-in-your-games-and-if-you-do-how?p=671815#post671815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Jason Statham? No, wait, he's british, forget it... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>You mean he's English.<br /> Both Scotland and England are parts of Great Britain, so both are British.<br /> Sorry, pet peeve :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I had a conscience once. Alas, I appear to have misplaced it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1309-andreas-rayne","name":"Andreas Rayne","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-09T05:22:23-08:00","id":761383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Andreas Rayne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/671583-sorcerers-do-you-use-those-guys-in-your-games-and-if-you-do-how?p=761127#post761127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You mean he's English.<br /> Both Scotland and England are parts of Great Britain, so both are British.<br /> Sorry, pet peeve :P</div> </div> </div> </div>It's fine, the mistake got totally through me. It's actually funny as usually don't forget that.<br /> At least i called no irishman or woman british. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}